# HeroTown

Shared rules for every coding agent on this project: Claude Code (reads this through `CLAUDE.md`), Cursor (reads a generated copy in `.cursor/rules/simulation-core.mdc`) and GPT/Codex (reads this file). Edit this file only, then run `npm run sync:rules`; a test fails if the Cursor copy is stale.

Village-building party RPG with idle auto-expeditions. Design source of truth: `Docs/마을 성장 RPG – 게임 디자인 문서(GDD).md` (Korean). Per-system notes live next to it (`Docs/village.md`, `Docs/dungeons.md`, `Docs/combat.md`, `Docs/classes.md`, `Docs/expedition.md`); update the matching note when a system's behavior changes.

## Working together

Several agents work on this repository. `Docs/tasks.md` is the shared task board: who owns each task, which files it touches, and its status. Before starting:

- Read your task in `Docs/tasks.md` and the "함께 일하는 규칙" section at its top.
- Run `git status`. If there are uncommitted changes you did not make, stop and tell the user: another agent is probably working.
- Touch only the files your task lists. `src/core`, `src/data` and the save format belong to one task at a time.

When done: `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm test` and `npm run build` pass, one commit per task, and the task's row in `Docs/tasks.md` says "완료 (commit hash)" with a short note.

Current stage: stage 1 (MVP) per GDD section 12. Stage 2+ systems (marriage, children, alchemy, cloud saves) stay out of scope until their stage.

## Commands

- `npm test` — vitest, all tests must pass
- `npx tsc --noEmit` — typecheck
- `npm run build` — typecheck + production build
- `npm run dev` — Vite dev server
- `npm run simulate` — prints the balance table (GDD 7.6)
- `npm run sync:rules` — copies this file into the Cursor rule

## Core rules

- `src/core` is pure TypeScript. It must not import React, the DOM, three.js, `src/ui`, or `src/locales`.
- Balance numbers live in `src/data` JSON. Core code reads those tables and does not hard-code tuning values.
- Every random roll in the core goes through `src/core/rng.ts`. Do not call `Math.random` there.
- Player-facing copy uses translation keys in `src/locales/en.json` and `src/locales/ko.json`. Both files keep the same key tree (`src/locales/parity.test.ts` checks this).
- Game changes go through `reduce` in `src/core/game.ts`. Combat stays behind `runDungeon`; village, time and save work call it and do not rewrite the combat loop.
- Save format changes bump `SAVE_VERSION` and add a migration in `migrate`.
- Add or update tests with each change; probability systems get seeded simulation tests.

## Graphics (GDD 11.7)

- Cute voxel 3D with three.js, all generated in code, no image assets. Code lives in `src/ui/voxel/`.
- `VillageScene.ts` draws the village from game state, `world.ts` holds lots, props and the gate, `character.ts` builds heroes and humanoid monsters, `enemies.ts` has one model per monster id, `BattleScene.ts` replays a `DungeonReport`, `replay.ts` turns the log into steps, `portrait.ts` renders hero, monster and dungeon pictures, `look.ts` derives looks from the hero id until genes exist.
- Build boxes through `Builder` in `kit.ts`. It merges boxes so each moving part is one draw call. Do not add one mesh per box.
- When adding a monster to `monsters.json`, add its model to `enemies.ts`.
- Battle replays need `dungeonId`, `party`, `floors` on the report and `actorId`/`targetId` in log params. Keep them when changing combat logging.
- The reference prototype is `prototypes/voxel3d/index.html` (open via `npm run dev`).

## UI

- Game-style shell in `src/ui/App.tsx`: the 3D village fills the screen; `Hud` on top, a dock of screens at the bottom, each screen opens in a framed `Window` (bottom sheet on phones). Tapping a building in 3D opens its screen (`BUILDING_SCREEN`).
- Screens: `src/ui/game/heroScreens.tsx` (inn, heroes, retirees), `src/ui/game/battleScreens.tsx` (dungeons, prep, party editor, chronicle), `src/ui/game/villageScreens.tsx` (town, smith, result, settings, absence, depart confirm). Shared parts (`Window`, `Res`, `Chip`, `Bar`, `Portrait`, `CostList`) are in `src/ui/game/kit.tsx`; icons in `src/ui/game/icons.tsx`.
- Notices from `reduce` show as toasts; `seenDeath`/`wornParty` show the depart confirm window. Dispatch through `apply` so this keeps working.
- Style tokens are on `:root` in `src/ui/styles.css`. Reuse `.btn` (`primary`, `gold`, `danger`, `ad`, `small`, `tiny`), `.card`, `.chip`, `.bar` rather than new one-off styles.
- Sounds are synthesized in `src/ui/sound.ts`; no audio files.

## Systems

- First-play guide: goals in `src/data/guide.json`, evaluated by `src/core/guide.ts` (`guideStatus`, `claimGuide`), shown by `GuideCard` in `App.tsx`.
- Expeditions take time (`Docs/expedition.md`): `depart` creates an `Expedition` from a party preset and settles it at `returnAt` in catchUp. Live panel: `src/ui/ExpeditionPanel.tsx` (seeks the replay to the clock); heroes away walk out through `GATE` in `world.ts` and back in (`VillageScene.syncAway`).
- Retirement: `retire` moves a hero (age ≥ `retirementRules.minAge`) into `state.retirees`; `assignRetiree` posts one retiree per building; `retireeBonus(state, building)` feeds the bonus into the matching system. Numbers in `src/data/retirement.json`.
- Strategy depth (Docs/depth.md): status effects live on combat units (poison is the old `dot`; paralysis, slow and silence roll only for monsters that have them, so older fights replay identically). Potions are a village stock (`state.potions`), brewed by the alchemy workshop (`src/core/alchemy.ts`, `src/data/alchemy.json`), carried per preset (`preset.supplies`) and returned unused after an expedition or auto run. `runDungeon(..., supplies)` reports `potionsUsed`. Stage 3b adds floor traps (`trapChance`; a rogue or the trapSense trinket disarms) and ambushing monsters (`ambush`; the alert trinket stops them). Trinkets are stash gear with `slot: 'trinket'` (two per hero), made by the magic workshop (`src/core/magic.ts`, `src/data/magic.json`) from the new `crystal` material. Stage 3c adds boss patterns: a monster with `blastEvery` charges (`log.charge`) and blasts `chargeTicks` later on its own clock; warriors, rogues and archers (`classes.json` `interrupt`) break it, and `tactics.blast: 'brace'` braces the whole party instead. Boss `phases` summon help and change the blast rhythm (`log.phase`, `log.summon`). Stage 3d: the dragon's nest draws two affixes and a lineup per floor each season (`src/core/nest.ts`, `src/data/nest.json`, `nestSeason(seed, calendar)`); `runDungeon(..., supplies, { floors, affixes })` applies them and reports `affixes`. `state.nestSeen` holds the revealed season key (rogue `scout`, guild `buyIntel`, or a returning trip). Skills (Docs/skills.md): role actions stay innate; learned skills add `effect`s from `classes.json` (`src/core/skills.ts`, `heroSkillEffects`). A hero keeps the innate skill plus two of three picks, opened at `training.json` `pickLevels`; `createHero` recomputes `skillPoints` from the level. The training ground (`src/core/drill.ts`, `state.drills`) gives catch-up XP and lets a hero `forget` a pick.
- Families (Docs/generations.md): rules in `src/core/family.ts`, numbers in `src/data/family.json`. Affinity lives in `state.bonds` (one entry per pair, a < b); `state.proposals` wait for the player's `acceptProposal`/`declineProposal`; season turns run `turnSeason` (affinity, proposals, conception) and `deliverBirths` adds children to the roster. Appearance genes are core data in `src/core/genes.ts`: `genesFor(hero)` returns stored genes or the id-drawn ones, and `src/ui/voxel/look.ts` only turns genes into a `Look`. Screens read families through `familyOf`, `topBonds`, `bondStage`, `population`, `housingFree`. When a year turns, `passAway` may send the old (60+, certain at the oldest age) to `state.graveyard`; graves keep cause, year, age, gender, family, parents, spouse and genes, and `legend` marks the hall of fame (`hallOfFame`, `familyLegends`, `legendBonus`, `ancestorsOf`).
- Growth and difficulty: each level-up adds training (+1 to every stat); each dungeon's `monsterScale` sets its difficulty for its `recommendedLevel`. Tier 1 dungeons cannot kill.
- Balance tools: `npx vite-node tools/print-curve.ts` (win rate by level per dungeon), `tools/tune-curve.ts` (finds `monsterScale` for target levels), `tools/first-hour.ts [minutes]` (plays the opening to catch dead ends). Re-run them after changing combat, growth or rewards.
